This product includes material from chompy by Jeff Arese
(https://github.com/jeffarese/chompy), licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0):

  - app/src/test/resources/screens/*.txt: Claude Code screen captures, unmodified.
  - The approach to reading and answering Claude Code's menus in
    app/src/main/java/dev/jwise/rhubarb/agent/ (ClaudeScreen.kt, PromptAnswers.kt): a menu counts
    only while it is live, the screen is read again before an answer is pressed, and digits wait
    out Claude Code's first ~600 ms. Rhubarb's code is its own, smaller implementation.
  - The design of the message box, the Claude Code controls strip and the "Needs you" board.

The terminal renderer is adapted from chuchu (https://github.com/jossephus/chuchu, MIT) and uses
Ghostty's terminal engine (MIT). The QR scanner is ZXing and zxing-android-embedded (Apache 2.0).
